#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:421
#: 220408f8c049440a97281a602f20d6cd
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:423
#: ea4dc64b63ee46398c7420a7d4ab04fa
msgid "RC input is configured on the PPM pin, at one end of the servo rail, marked RC in the above diagram. This pin supports all unidirectional RC protocols including PPM.  The DSM/SBUS pin is also tied to the PPM pin. For CRSF/ELRS/etc. protocols, a full UART will need to be used with its SERIALx_PROTOCOL set to \"23\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:426
#: f8996c3822dc4da5a6120ab9d618a207
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:428
#: 821509e6f4c14cfdba9722c6f60f2c5b
msgid "The MUPilot supports up to 14 PWM outputs. First first 8 outputs (labeled \"M1 to M8\") are controlled by a dedicated STM32F103 IO controller. These 8 outputs support all PWM output formats, but not DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:432
#: 0d90d1a943cc4f5ba064c56a010be45f
msgid "The remaining 6 outputs (labeled A1 to A6) are the \"auxiliary\" outputs. These are directly attached to the STM32F765 and support all PWM protocols as well as DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:436
#: 1ae050296c5148028ef3e742200a232e
msgid "All 14 PWM outputs have GND on the top row, 5V on the middle row and signal on the bottom row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:439
#: 0330b4cdaff74c2a890f51dbb4c92971
msgid "The 8 main PWM outputs are in 3 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:441
#: 23a1a57ee28d41318897ee1c14a1944c
msgid "PWM 1 and 2 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:442
#: 85c4aef5be524e87a97de60dabe28a86
msgid "PWM 3 and 4 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:443
#: 40b5e08116b34fe7b6a3d4345ed4376a
msgid "PWM 5, 6, 7 and 8 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:445
#: 7ccc9f74967f4c21ba6436b22a14c38f
msgid "The 6 auxiliary PWM outputs are in 2 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:447
#: 4ab40d9e594e4ac6909cd41cf73b061a
msgid "PWM 1, 2, 3 and 4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:448
#: 094b86b9bc6f4517be9125d2af34317c
msgid "PWM 5 and 6 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:450
#: 5c7d00c9bf8547f9bd36d3e9ca1a6ecf
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:454
#: a591380e9f264bb98f4d643ff110c8a5
msgid "The output levels of the auxiliary outputs can be selected by switch to be either 3.3V or 5V. The output level is 3.3V for the main outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:457
#: 338b55d3e4b247e6b5c05e7685b32dd3
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:458
#: ae9a3ee05f2147cc8294dc144e55911f
msgid "The board has two dedicated power monitor ports on 6 pin connectors. The correct battery setting parameters are dependent on the type of power brick which is connected. The first is analog only, the second may be either analog or I2C, depending on baseboard jumpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:460
#: 4310b86d86e043b7956297c7d7356a6d
msgid "In order to enable monitoring, the :ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` or :ref:`BATT2_MONITOR<BATT2_MONITOR>` parameter must be set. By default :ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` is set to \"4\" for the included power module.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:462
#: 4715a510fc2c420c95e3caf4fc8b6695
msgid "Default params for the first monitor are set and are: * :ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 2 * :ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 1 * :ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 18.0 * :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 24.0 (may need adjustment if supplied monitor is not used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:469
#: d9207954e9fd46daa1933ed5fc3c2fbe
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:470
#: 2b81756ebad941d1962e4bd044df082e
msgid "The MUPilot has a builtin IST8310 compass. Due to potential interference the board is usually used with an external I2C compass as part of a GPS/Compass combination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:473
#: 11ffd8d7cda34c03b04afd6e8b8e3d2f
msgid "GPIOs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:474
#: 7414b328c68f40e1b34b7924a4a9d24e
msgid "The 6 auxiliary outputs can be used as GPIOs (relays, buttons, RPM etc). To use them see :ref:`common-gpios`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:476
#: 2874a0e3231148f59c50053105742c82
msgid "The numbering of the GPIOs for PIN variables in ArduPilot is: * MAIN1 101 * MAIN2 102 * MAIN3 103 * MAIN4 104 * MAIN5 105 * MAIN6 106 * MAIN7 107 * MAIN8 108 * AUX1 50 * AUX2 51 * AUX3 52 * AUX4 53 * AUX5 54 * AUX6 55"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:493
#: c89a2344e7304a74b02c6ec5be627de2
msgid "Analog inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:495
#: 9e6d3c858c2348c88e1b8f428179b176
msgid "The MUPilot has 7 analog inputs * ADC Pin0 -> Battery Voltage * ADC Pin1 -> Battery Current Sensor * ADC Pin2 -> Battery Voltage 2 * ADC Pin3 -> Battery Current Sensor 2 * ADC Pin4 -> ADC port pin 2 * ADC Pin14 -> ADC port pin 3 * ADC Pin10 -> Board 5V Sense * ADC Pin11 -> Board 3.3V Sense * ADC Pin103 -> RSSI voltage monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:507
#: 2e6ed5b7a27845ff90a97c3a8eba72b0
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MUPilot.rst:508
#: 895141890bd2419084dea1253cb06561
msgid "The board comes pre-installed with an ArduPilot compatible bootloader, allowing the loading of \\*.apj firmware files with any ArduPilot compatible ground station."
msgstr ""
